# EXPECT: spawn with an observed/temporal function
#
# (round 108) Part 2a routes an OBSERVED function's locals through the
# process-global env BY NAME; two OS threads then race one slot while
# first-observation grows the obs array: "undefined variable 'seen'" then
# SIGSEGV rc 139 where the VM prints 4000 / 4000. Lower contention is
# worse -- silent wrong counts at rc 0. Keyed on ANY observed function in
# the program, not on the spawn argument (the function value can flow
# dynamically).
define reader() as:
    local seen is 0
    for i in range of 4000:
        seen is seen + 1
        r is report of seen
    return seen

h1 is spawn of reader
h2 is spawn of reader
t1 is thread_join of h1
t2 is thread_join of h2
print of t1
print of t2
